v {xschem version=3.4.8RC file_version=1.2
*
* mini-MOSbius NMOS differential-pair tail current bank (TODO.md Sec 2,
* closed 2026-08-22). One drawn pin, `d` -- wire it to the shared source
* node of the two mosbius_nmos halves it biases. Drawing it there IS what
* declares them a pair: the router claims the two same-polarity FETs
* sourced on that net as ndiffpair+/ndiffpair- instead of inferring the
* pairing, and `tail=2/4/6/8` reaches ctrl_dpn_tail, which nothing else
* can set.
*
* Drawing no mosbius_ntail at all keeps today's behaviour exactly: the
* two mosbius_nmos halves' shared source is tied straight to VGND by
* ctrl_dpn_source, usable as two standalone FETs (CLAUDE.md Traps #3).
*
* Gate and source are NOT drawn, and that is not a style choice: the
* bank's gate really is `ibias`, the same reference the whole bias chain
* hangs off, and its source really is VGND -- both hard-wired on
* silicon, so both are supplied through xschem's `extra` mechanism like
* every other implicit pin in this library (see mosbius_nsink.sym's
* header). Override per instance with g=<net>/s=<net> if you ever need
* to.
*
*
* This symbol holds ONE transistor: the mirror slave. The reference leg
* it copies lives once per chip, in mini_mosbius.sch's bias generator,
* the same way the chip has one mirror_n reference feeding every
* programmable leg. Until 2026-08-28 every one of these symbols carried
* its own private reference diode, so N devices on a sheet split the
* chip's one reference current N ways: two mosbius_nsink at ratio=2
* measured -99 uA each where -200 uA was right.
*
* Drawn as what it is: one transistor with a fixed gate. The gate and the
* rail end are terminated, not open stubs -- they are supplied through
* `extra` and there is no pin box on either, so there is nothing to wire
* and nothing a wire could silently miss. Only the drain has a pin.
*
* It is deliberately not an ideal-current-source circle any more. This is
* a mirror leg: its current droops with output voltage (about 12 uA/V,
* ~85 kOhm) and collapses as the drain approaches its rail. A current
* source glyph promises behaviour the hardware does not have; see
* examples/currentsource/ for the measured I-V curve.
*
* The pin-box (B) record below is declared in netlist pin order, which
* is also the .subckt port order -- extra pins are appended, in the
* order `extra` lists them. mosbius/netlist.py's DEVICE_PINS holds a
* matching copy -- change both together.
}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@spiceprefix@name @pinlist @g @s @symname tail=@tail"
template="name=X1 tail=2 g=ibias s=VGND spiceprefix=X"
extra="g s"
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
L 4 -15 -30 -15 30 {}
L 4 -15 -20 0 -20 {}
L 4 0 -30 0 -20 {}
L 4 0 -40 0 -30 {}
L 4 -15 20 0 20 {}
L 4 0 20 0 30 {}
L 4 -10 30 10 30 {}
L 4 -6 34 6 34 {}
L 4 -2 38 2 38 {}
L 4 -25 -15 -25 15 {}
L 4 -40 0 -25 0 {}
P 4 5 -43 -3 -37 -3 -37 3 -43 3 -43 -3 {fill=true}
B 5 -2.5 -42.5 2.5 -37.5 {name=d dir=inout}
T {@name} 24 -17 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
T {tail=@tail} 24 1 0 0 0.15 0.15 {}
T {@g} -70 -8 0 0 0.26 0.26 {layer=1}
T {@s} 14 30 0 0 0.26 0.26 {layer=1}
T {@#0:net_name} 6 -52 0 0 0.15 0.15 {layer=15 hide=instance}
